em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.5806em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">u</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2806em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> with feedback <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>0.5</mn><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_t=-0.5x_t</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.5806em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">u</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2806em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7944em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">0.5</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2806em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> stable?","explanation":"The closed loop is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.7</mn><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_{t+1}=0.7x_t</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6389em;vertical-align:-0.2083em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2083em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7944em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.7</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2806em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mn>0.7</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|0.7|\\lt1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∣0.7∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">&lt;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>.","type":"tf","answer":true},{"id":"robot-control-3","prompt":"What does model predictive control do at every time step?","explanation":"Re-planning with each new measurement handles disturbances and constraints.","type":"single","options":["Optimizes a short-horizon control sequence under constraints and applies only the first action","Applies a fixed gain forever","Trains a neural network","Waits for the error to grow"],"answer":0},{"id":"robot-control-4","prompt":"In LQR, increasing the control cost matrix <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbf R</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">R</span></span></span></span> makes the controller…","explanation":"<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbf R</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">R</span></span></span></span> penalizes large control inputs.","type":"single","options":["gentler, using less effort and tracking more slowly","more aggressive","unstable","ignore the state"],"answer":0}],"motion-planning":[{"id":"motion-planning-1","prompt":"When is A* guaranteed to find the shortest path?","explanation":"With <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h=0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span> A* becomes Dijkstra, which is also optimal but slower.","type":"single","options":["When its heuristic never overestimates the remaining cost (admissible)","Always, with any heuristic","Only on graphs with no obstacles","Only with a zero heuristic"],"answer":0},{"id":"motion-planning-2","prompt":"Why are sampling-based planners like RRT preferred for 7-joint arms?","explanation":"RRT is probabilistically complete; RRT* also converges toward optimal.","type":"single","options":["Grids grow exponentially with dimension, while sampling only explores where it goes","RRT always finds the optimal path","Grids cannot represent obstacles","RRT needs no collision checking"],"answer":0},{"id":"motion-planning-3","prompt":"What does RRT* add to RRT?","explanation":"Plain RRT finds feasible but jagged, suboptimal paths.","type":"single","options":["A heuristic function","Rewiring nearby nodes to cheaper parents so paths converge toward optimal","A grid","A neural network"],"answer":1}],"robot-learning":[{"id":"robot-learning-1","prompt":"What is domain randomization?","explanation":"If the real world falls inside the training range, the policy transfers.","type":"single","options":["Randomizing simulator physics and visuals so a policy works across many variations, including reality","Randomly choosing which robot to use","Adding noise to rewards","Training on random labels"],"answer":0},{"id":"robot-learning-2","prompt":"Why do diffusion policies help imitation learning from human demonstrations?","explanation":"Averaging \"go left\" and \"go right\" with MSE produces an invalid \"go straight\".","type":"single","options":["They model multi-modal action distributions instead of averaging modes","They are faster than MLPs","They need no data","They remove the need for cameras"],"answer":0},{"id":"robot-learning-3","prompt":"What does a vision-language-action model output?","explanation":"VLAs start from vision-language models and are fine-tuned on robot data.","type":"single","options":["Captions","Robot actions conditioned on images and an instruction","Depth maps only","Reward values"],"answer":1}],"__exam":[{"id":"robotics-exam-1","prompt":"A robot localizes with GPS (noise std 3 m) and wheel odometry that drifts. Which approach fuses them best?","explanation":"The filter weights each source by its uncertainty over time.","type":"single","options":["A Kalman filter (or EKF) that predicts with odometry and updates with GPS","Averaging the two positions","Using only GPS","Using only odometry"],"answer":0},{"id":"robotics-exam-2","prompt":"Order the classical stack: perception and estimation, planning, control. Which runs at the highest frequency?","explanation":"Control loops often run at hundreds or thousands of hertz; planners much more slowly.","type":"single","options":["Route planning","Behaviour planning","Low-level control","Map building"],"answer":2},{"id":"robotics-exam-3","prompt":"A learned locomotion policy works perfectly in simulation and falls over on the real robot. Which techniques address this? (select all)","explanation":"These are the standard sim-to-real tools.","type":"multi","options":["Domain randomization","System identification of real parameters","A privileged teacher distilled into a sensor-only student","Training longer in the same simulator settings"],"answer":[0,1,2]},{"id":"robotics-exam-4","prompt":"A drone's altitude oscillates more and more after a gain change. What is the most likely cause?","explanation":"Too much gain pushes closed-loop poles outside the stable region.","type":"single","options":["The proportional (or integral) gain is too high, making the loop unstable","The derivative gain is too high","The sensor is perfect","The target is too low"],"answer":0}]}